        "Must be taken within the first year as an Applied Computer Science or Computer Science major.",
        "For each pair of courses referenced, only one of them may be used towards any degree requirements.",
        "ECE 445 may be taken as a replacement for CS 465 .",
        "At most 3 credits total of CS 491 Industry-Sponsored Senior Design Project may be counted toward the senior computer science requirement.",
        "At most 6 credits total of CS 499 Special Topics in Computer Science may be counted toward the senior computer science requirement.",
        "MATH 446 and OR 481 are equivalent, and cannot both be counted towards the requirements.",
        "Only Bachelor's to Accelerated Master's Program and CS Honors Program students are eligible to enroll in graduate courses identified for those programs, including: CS 540 , CS 550 , CS 551 , CS 555 , CS 571 , CS 580 , CS 583 , CS 584 , CS 587 , SWE 619 , SWE 637 , SWE 642 . Only one of each pair of courses may be used for any requirements of this degree: CS 440 and CS 540 ; CS 450 and CS 550 ; CS 451 and CS 551 ; CS 455 and CS 555 ; CS 471 and CS 571 ; CS 480 and CS 580 ; CS 483 and CS 583 ; CS 484 and CS 584 ; CS 487 and CS 587 ; SWE 419 and SWE 619 ; SWE 437 and SWE 637 ; SWE 432 and SWE 642 .",
        "Those who take MATH 352 Statistics may replace STAT 344 Probability and Statistics for Engineers and Scientists I with MATH 351 Probability .",
        "Those planning to take MATH 352 Statistics may replace STAT 344 Probability and Statistics for Engineers and Scientists I with MATH 351 Probability .",
        "None of CS 504 , CS 530 , or CS 531 may be used towards this degree."
